# The window: XTWINOPS reports, the operations a host must allow, the title and the icon name, the
# title stack and the title modes.

test XTWINOPS reports the text area, the cell and the window state
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI 14 t text area in pixels, 16 t cell in pixels, 18 t text area in characters, 11 t window state, 13 t position
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
size 20 5
feed \e[18t\e[11t\e[13t
reply \e[8;5;20t\e[1t\e[3;0;0t
feed \e[14t\e[16t
reply~ \e[4;*;*t\e[6;*;*t

test the window title is not reported unless the host allows it
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI 21 t reports the title; xterm leaves it off by default as a program's title is text of its choosing
size 20 5
feed \e]2;secret\a\e[21t\e[20t
reply none

test the window title is not reported with the window operations on either
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI 21 t reports the title; here a switch of its own, off by default
window-ops allow
size 20 5
feed \e]2;secret\a\e[21t\e[20t
reply none

test the title and the icon name are reported when the host allows it
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI 20 t is OSC L icon ST, CSI 21 t is OSC l title ST; OSC 0 sets both, OSC 1 the icon name, OSC 2 the title
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
title-report allow
size 20 5
feed \e]0;both\a\e[20t\e[21t
reply \e]Lboth\e\\\e]lboth\e\\
feed \e]1;icon\a\e]2;title\a\e[20t\e[21t
reply \e]Licon\e\\\e]ltitle\e\\

test controls are taken out of a title when it is set
convention C0, DEL and C1 controls are dropped from a title when it is set, so none is drawn or reported (xterm replaces them in the report)
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
title-report allow
size 20 5
feed \e]2;a\u{85}b\a\e[21t
reply \e]lab\e\\

test the title stack keeps the title and the icon name together or apart
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI 22 ; Ps t saves (0 both, 1 icon name, 2 title), CSI 23 ; Ps t restores
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
title-report allow
size 20 5
feed \e]1;i1\a\e]2;t1\a\e[22;0t\e]1;i2\a\e]2;t2\a\e[23;1t\e[20t\e[21t
reply \e]Li1\e\\\e]lt2\e\\
feed \e[23;2t\e[21t
reply \e]lt2\e\\

test a pop takes the slot that holds what it asks for
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI 22 and 23 with the icon name and the title saved by separate pushes
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
title-report allow
size 20 5
feed \e]1;i1\a\e]2;t1\a\e[22;1t\e[22;2t\e]1;x\a\e]2;y\a\e[23;0t\e[20t\e[21t
reply \e]Li1\e\\\e]lt1\e\\

test the title modes read and report in hexadecimal
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI > Ps t sets title modes, 0 hexadecimal set, 1 hexadecimal query; CSI > Ps T resets
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
title-report allow
size 20 5
feed \e[>0;1t\e]2;6162\a\e[21t
reply \e]l6162\e\\
feed \e[>0;1T\e[21t
reply \e]lab\e\\

test a full reset clears the title modes and the stack
spec xterm ctlseqs: RIS
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
title-report allow
size 20 5
feed \e[>0;1t\ec\e]2;ab\a\e[21t
reply \e]lab\e\\

test the window operations do nothing unless the host allows them
spec xterm ctlseqs: window manipulation is controlled by the allowWindowOps resource, which is off by default
size 20 5
feed \e[8;10;40t\e[18t
reply \e[8;5;20t

test the sizes in cells take effect at once when allowed
convention the engine resizes to the size asked for before the host has changed its window, so that the program reads the size it asked for (esctest2 DECRQSS_DECSLPP)
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
window-ops allow
size 20 5
feed \e[8;10;40t\e[18t
reply \e[8;10;40t
feed \e[27t\e[18t\eP$qt\e\\
reply \e[8;27;40t\eP1$r27t\e\\
feed \e[24*|\eP$q*|\e\\
reply \eP1$r24*|\e\\

test DECSNLS and DECSLPP are refused unless the host allows them
spec VT510 DECSNLS, DECSLPP: change the number of lines; here a window operation
size 20 5
feed \e[24*|\e[40t\e[18t
reply \e[8;5;20t

test a size past what the screen holds is cut
convention a program asking for more cells than the host's screen has gets what fits, and without a screen the engine cuts at 500
known-fail: alacritty – no window operations or title reports: only CSI 18 t is answered
window-ops allow
size 20 5
feed \e[8;9999;9999t\e[18t
reply \e[8;500;500t
